WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.479 --> 00:00:02.256
(peaceful orchestral music)

00:00:02.256 --> 00:00:05.059
- When people say they
summit for the view,

00:00:05.059 --> 00:00:07.532
I think they're missing
a lot of the equation

00:00:07.532 --> 00:00:10.032
of why we do the things we do.

00:00:12.043 --> 00:00:15.293
The summit, honestly, is
pretty anti-climactic.

00:00:15.293 --> 00:00:17.398
(grunting)

00:00:17.398 --> 00:00:21.398
The movement is, for me,
the most exciting part.

00:00:22.852 --> 00:00:25.131
(deep exhale)
My name is Erik Weihenmayer,

00:00:25.131 --> 00:00:26.722
and I'm the first blind person

00:00:26.722 --> 00:00:29.704
to have climbed the tallest
peak in every continent.

00:00:29.704 --> 00:00:32.037
(whooshing)

00:00:36.177 --> 00:00:39.212
(moves into dedicated optimistic music)

00:00:39.212 --> 00:00:40.525
When I was four or five years old,

00:00:40.525 --> 00:00:43.242
I was diagnosed with this
incredibly rare disease

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:44.809
called Retinoschisis.

00:00:44.809 --> 00:00:49.801
It attacked my retinas and
essentially unraveled them.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.262
When I finally went blind,
(rustling)

00:00:51.262 --> 00:00:54.156
it was a weird relief, like
the worst thing had happened,

00:00:54.156 --> 00:00:56.823
so there's nothing else to lose.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.172
There was a recreational group

00:00:59.172 --> 00:01:01.035
taking blind kids rock climbing,

00:01:01.035 --> 00:01:03.749
(clanking)
and that was it for me.

00:01:03.749 --> 00:01:07.400
It was sort of the full
package of adventure,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.950
all the things I thought I
wouldn't have as a blind person.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:13.472
(clanking)

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:15.840
- You need 14 for this pitch?

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.932
- [Erik] Yeah, I'm counting 'em right now.

00:01:17.932 --> 00:01:19.099
- [Climber] K.

00:01:21.096 --> 00:01:22.733
- When I get onto a rock face,

00:01:22.733 --> 00:01:26.316
I actually feel like I'm in my element.

00:01:26.316 --> 00:01:29.488
The things that sighted people
learn to do with their eyes,

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:31.988
I’ve learned to do with my hands.

00:01:33.717 --> 00:01:36.907
When I'm clipping a bolt to a carabiner,

00:01:36.907 --> 00:01:39.986
I'm feeling it, I'm making
sure it's correctly clipped,

00:01:39.986 --> 00:01:44.153
and if I fall, that that
carabiner is gonna hold me.

00:01:46.221 --> 00:01:48.819
I can't look up the rock, and see

00:01:48.819 --> 00:01:52.278
the holds, and plan a big route.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:55.094
I can only see as far as my hands.

00:01:55.094 --> 00:01:57.883
It's breathtakingly exciting.

00:01:57.883 --> 00:02:01.127
(clanking)
Sometimes you hear those cars

00:02:01.127 --> 00:02:04.960
way down below you in
the floor of the canyon.

00:02:06.798 --> 00:02:09.381
I love that sound of emptiness.

00:02:10.522 --> 00:02:13.031
A lot of external stuff
sort of disappears,

00:02:13.031 --> 00:02:15.019
and you're thinking about nothing

00:02:15.019 --> 00:02:17.936
but that next hold in front of you.

00:02:19.512 --> 00:02:21.744
So it's very, very meditative,

00:02:21.744 --> 00:02:25.327
very much kind of like
an inner mind sport.

00:02:26.615 --> 00:02:28.215
(whooshing)

00:02:28.215 --> 00:02:29.048
(clacking)
I like that,

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:31.023
I think that's the best pitch.

00:02:31.023 --> 00:02:33.797
- Could you feel that space,
like, the exposure down there?

00:02:33.797 --> 00:02:35.780
- Yeah, I mean, especially
with these trucks

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:38.063
flyin' by down there; it kinda echoes

00:02:38.063 --> 00:02:40.714
through the whole canyon,
and you can hear everything.

00:02:40.714 --> 00:02:41.547
- Yeah.

00:02:41.547 --> 00:02:43.269
What do you say we top out?

00:02:43.269 --> 00:02:44.102
- Yeah, let's summit.

00:02:44.102 --> 00:02:44.935
It's right up here, right?

00:02:44.935 --> 00:02:45.768
- Yeah.

00:02:45.768 --> 00:02:46.601
- Okay.

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:50.768
(peaceful spacey music)
(clanking)

00:02:54.588 --> 00:02:57.413
As a blind climber, it's really hard,

00:02:57.413 --> 00:03:01.580
and you just sorta have
to embrace that suffering.

00:03:03.732 --> 00:03:06.832
Blindness is just a thing
that happened to me.

00:03:06.832 --> 00:03:08.928
I think, like all adversities,

00:03:08.928 --> 00:03:11.293
we gotta use them as a catalyst

00:03:11.293 --> 00:03:13.793
to push you in new directions.

00:03:14.965 --> 00:03:17.859
It's the idea of turning
bad things into good things,

00:03:17.859 --> 00:03:21.526
and it's something I
think we all could use.

